    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on exploiting favorable matchups against volatile arms. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.66) represent our strongest daily plays, both benefiting from a combination of prime lineup positioning and high-ceiling matchups against Lorenzen and L\u00f3pez, respectively. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically capitalizes on a massive +14% park boost and +19% SP skill advantage, making him our primary engine for Runs and RBI today. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** (65.85) and **Nasim Nunez** (68.26) are high-leverage starts despite batting in the leadoff or back-end spots, as both gain significant value from today\u2019s park factors and the underlying weaknesses of Lorenzen and Avila.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the benching of **Jacob Wilson** (50.44) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.33). While both carry respectable scores, they were squeezed out by the sheer efficiency of our middle infield and utility slots. **Jacob Wilson** was penalized by the opposing pitcher's elite skill metrics, and the decision to start **Curtis Mead** (62.15) over **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** was driven by the optimizer\u2019s preference for **Curtis Mead**'s superior platoon alignment against Lorenzen. Meanwhile, we are forced to navigate the absence of **Gunnar Henderson**, whose game was postponed; ensure he is locked in your bench to avoid wasted daily caps. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that **Kyle Tucker** (53.64) is facing the formidable Wheeler. While **Kyle Tucker** is an essential anchor, the -19% SP skill penalty significantly dampens his outlook compared to his typical baseline. Additionally, keep a close eye on **Luis Robert Jr.** (48.49); his score is suppressed today by a negative platoon dynamic and an elite hold from the opposing pitcher Sproat, which limits his stolen base ceiling. We are betting that the volume of high-score utility options like **Sam Antonacci** (63.68) and **Drake Baldwin** (63.19) will provide the necessary floor to overcome the tougher matchups faced by our elite power hitters.",
